+!>@brief mapn_tracer_dry: remap all tracers as in Lagrangian_to_Eulerian (water results unchanged), then remap the
+!! dry tracers' dry ratio c = q/(1-sum water) over dry-air thickness: old layers dp1*(1-old water), new layers
+!! dp2*(1-remapped water), edges rescaled to the old column dry mass. Returns q = c*D2/dp2, so a uniform c stays
+!! uniform and sum(q*dp) is conserved as by the moist remap. Dry edges are cumulative sums near 1e5 Pa, so they are
+!! kept in R_GRID (a 32-bit edge would cost ulp(1e5 Pa)/D in thin layers, ~1e-4 at the surface).
+ subroutine mapn_tracer_dry(nq, nwat, ndry, km, pe1, pe2, q1, dp2, kord, j,     &
+                            i1, i2, isd, ied, jsd, jed, fill, dry_tr)
+      integer, intent(in):: km, j, nq, nwat, ndry, i1, i2, isd, ied, jsd, jed
+      integer, intent(in):: kord(nq)
